# Cloudflare Pages → nowssb (this site) → Settings → Variables and Secrets → Production
# Names only — never commit real values. Add each as an encrypted "Secret".
#
# ── Google Play Billing (functions/api/play/verify.js, functions/api/play/rtdn.js) ──
# Google Cloud service account JSON (whole file). Invite its email in
# Play Console → Users and permissions with app access to NowssB and the
# permissions "View financial data, orders, and cancellation survey responses"
# and "Manage orders and subscriptions". The Google Play Android Developer API
# must be enabled in that service account's Google Cloud project.
PLAY_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=
# Firebase console → Project settings → Service accounts → Generate new private
# key (project nowssb-34f1b); paste the whole JSON. Used for Firestore REST.
FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT=
# Same kind of JSON, used by /api/push and /api/users (FCM). The Play functions
# fall back to it when FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT is absent.
FCM_SERVICE_ACCOUNT=
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=nowssb-34f1b
#
# ── Cloudflare R2 media uploads (functions/api/admin/upload-url.js) ──
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
R2_BUCKET=
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
R2_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://media.nowssb.com
#
# Until the Play variables exist, /api/play/* answers 501 naming what is
# missing and the app says purchases are not available — nothing is granted.
# Offline test: node tools/play/play-functions.test.mjs
#
# Real-time Developer Notifications (optional, recommended — renewals,
# cancellations, expiry): Google Cloud → Pub/Sub → create topic (e.g.
# play-rtdn); give google-play-developer-notifications@system.gserviceaccount.com
# the "Pub/Sub Publisher" role on it; Play Console → Monetization setup →
# Real-time developer notifications → that topic. Then add a PUSH subscription
# on the topic: endpoint https://nowssb.com/api/play/rtdn, "Enable
# authentication" with the PLAY_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON service account, audience
# left empty (defaults to the endpoint URL).
